/// Talos strategic merge patch directives.
///
/// Talos deletes from the machine configuration whatever a patch marks with `$patch: delete`:
///
/// | To delete | Write | Renders as |
/// | --- | --- | --- |
/// | a field, a map entry or a whole list | `mtu = patch.deleted` | `mtu: {$patch: delete}` |
/// | a list item | ``new { address = "10.0.0.3/24"; `$patch` = "delete" }`` | `- {address: 10.0.0.3/24, $patch: delete}` |
/// | a document | ``new LinkConfig { name = "eth0"; `$patch` = "delete" }`` | the document's `apiVersion`, `kind`, `name` and `$patch: delete` |
///
/// Talos rules that `ConfigPatch.pkl` checks before rendering:
/// - Talos matches a list item on its first property other than `$patch`, so a list item to delete
///   sets exactly one property.
/// - Talos cannot delete a key inside a list item.
/// - An object or document marked with `$patch: delete` is deleted as a whole, so it sets no other
///   property, apart from the `apiVersion`, `kind` and `name` that identify a document.
/// - The legacy `v1alpha1` document cannot be deleted as a whole, so it has no `$patch` property.
module talos.patch

/// The value of a `$patch` directive. Talos supports `delete` only.
typealias Directive = "delete"

/// A value that deletes the field or map entry it is assigned to.
///
/// Use [deleted] rather than creating instances.
class Delete {
  fixed `$patch`: Directive = "delete"
}

/// Deletes the field, map entry or list it is assigned to, as in `mtu = patch.deleted`.
fixed deleted: Delete = new {}

/// A value of type [T], or [deleted].
///
/// Every property of a generated document or class accepts [Delete], so that a patch can delete it.
/// The generated modules spell the union out, as in `mtu: (Int | patch.Delete)?`, so that type
/// errors name the expected type. Use this alias for the same purpose in your own modules.
typealias Patchable<T> = *T | Delete
